   "Foodlink F&B Holdings (India) Limited": "Bidding is open until 30 November at Rs 181-191, with Rs 14,898 for one lot of 78 shares. Retail demand is 2.33x but institutions are only 1.01x, and they often bid on the last day, so the early picture says little. Rs 192 crore of the Rs 361 crore issue is fresh money for the company. A DRHP match was not found. Re-check on the final day before deciding; a minimum lot is only a small bet if you accept losing it.",
   "Airpro Technology India Limited": "This SME issue opened today at Rs 99, closing 1 December, with no subscription data yet. One lot is 1,200 shares, or Rs 1,18,800, which is large. SME stocks trade thinly and swing sharply, so risk is higher. About Rs 29 crore of the Rs 36 crore issue is fresh money. A DRHP match was not found. Wait for demand numbers; a minimum lot is not a small bet here.",
   "Matangi Rubber Limited": "This mainboard issue opens 1 December at Rs 163-172, with Rs 14,964 for one lot of 87 shares. Rs 99 crore of the Rs 125 crore issue is fresh money. No subscription data exists yet, and demand is the main signal. Wait for the first days of bidding, especially institutional interest, before deciding. A minimum lot is a modest bet only if you can afford to lose it.",
   "A J Packaging Limited": "This SME issue opens 1 December at Rs 175-180, with one lot of 800 shares costing Rs 1,44,000, which is large. No subscription data is out yet. SME stocks trade thinly and can swing far more than mainboard shares. Rs 49.5 crore of the Rs 54 crore issue is fresh money. A DRHP match was not found. Wait for demand numbers; one lot is not a small bet.",
   "Monomark Engineering (India) Limited": "This mainboard issue opens 2 December at Rs 60-65, with Rs 14,625 for one lot of 225 shares. The whole Rs 175.5 crore issue is fresh money for the company. No subscription data exists yet, and a DRHP match was not found. Wait to see demand once bidding opens before deciding. A minimum lot is a modest bet only if you can accept losing it."
